  rules: [
    "1️⃣ INDIRECT QUESTIONS — EGRI SO'ROQLAR\n\nIndirect questions — so'roqni muloyimroq qilib ifodalash. To'g'ri so'roq (direct question) o'rniga ishlatiladi.\n\n📍 DIRECT (to'g'ri): Where is the station?\n📍 INDIRECT (egri): Can you tell me where the station is?\n\n📍 ASOSIY FARQ:\n  — Direct question: yordamchi fe'l + ega (verb + subject)\n  — Indirect question: ega + fe'l (subject + verb) — darak gapdagi kabi!\n\n📍 INDIRECT QUESTION TUZILISHI:\n  [So'roq iborasi] + [wh-word/if/whether] + [subject] + [verb]\n  📍 Can you tell me + where + the station + is?\n  📍 Do you know + if + she + is coming?\n\n📍 MUHIM: Indirect question oxirida QUESTION MARK bo'ladi (so'roq iborasi sababli).\n  📍 Can you tell me what time it is? (Soat necha ekanligini ayta olasizmi?)\n  📍 I wonder where he lives. (U qayerda yashaydi, deb o'ylayman — nuqta, chunki 'I wonder' darak gap)",
    "2️⃣ WH- WORDS BILAN INDIRECT QUESTIONS\n\nWh- words (what, where, when, why, who, how) bilan egri so'roqlar.\n\n📍 STRUKTURA:\n  [Intro phrase] + [wh-word] + [subject] + [verb]\n\n📍 WHERE:\n  📍 Direct: Where is the station?\n  📍 Indirect: Can you tell me where the station is? (not 'where is the station')\n  📍 Direct: Where does she live?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know where she lives? (not 'where does she live')\n\n📍 WHAT:\n  📍 Direct: What time is it?\n  📍 Indirect: Can you tell me what time it is?\n  📍 Direct: What does he want?\n  📍 Indirect: I wonder what he wants.\n\n📍 WHY:\n  📍 Direct: Why is she late?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know why she is late?\n  📍 Direct: Why did he leave?\n  📍 Indirect: Can you explain why he left?\n\n📍 HOW:\n  📍 Direct: How much does it cost?\n  📍 Indirect: Can you tell me how much it costs?\n  📍 Direct: How long have you been here?\n  📍 Indirect: I wonder how long you have been here.",
    "3️⃣ YES/NO QUESTIONS — IF / WHETHER\n\nYes/No savollari (javobi 'ha' yoki 'yo'q' bo'lgan) indirect qilinganda IF yoki WHETHER ishlatiladi.\n\n📍 IF BILAN:\n  📍 Direct: Is she coming?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know if she is coming?\n  📍 Direct: Does he like coffee?\n  📍 Indirect: Can you tell me if he likes coffee?\n\n📍 WHETHER BILAN (rasmiyroq, ikki variant):\n  📍 Direct: Is she coming or not?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know whether she is coming (or not)?\n  📍 Direct: Does he want tea or coffee?\n  📍 Indirect: I wonder whether he wants tea or coffee.\n\n📍 IF VS WHETHER:\n  📍 If = umumiy (kundalik)\n  📍 Whether = rasmiyroq, ikkala variantni ko'rsatganda\n  📍 Do you know if she is coming? (kundalik)\n  📍 I wonder whether she is coming or not. (ikki variant)\n\n📍 MUHIM: Indirect qilinganda do/does/did qatnashmaydi!\n  📍 Direct: Does she live here?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know if she lives here? (does YO'Q!)",
    "4️⃣ INTRO PHRASES — KIRISH SO'ZLARI\n\nIndirect question uchun ishlatiladigan kirish iboralari.\n\n📍 CAN / COULD / WOULD (muloyim so'roq):\n  📍 Can you tell me...? (Ayta olasizmi...)\n  📍 Could you tell me...? (Aytolmaysizmi... — muloyim)\n  📍 Would you mind telling me...? (Aytishga qarshi emassizmi...)\n  📍 Do you think you could tell me...? (Aytolmaysizmi deb o'ylaysiz...)\n\n📍 DO YOU KNOW / HAVE YOU ANY IDEA:\n  📍 Do you know...? (Bilasizmi...)\n  📍 Do you have any idea...? (Biror fikringiz bormi...)\n  📍 Do you happen to know...? (Tasodifan bilasizmi...)\n\n📍 I WONDER / I'M WONDERING (o'ylayapman):\n  📍 I wonder... (Qiziq...)\n  📍 I was wondering... (Qiziq edi...)\n  📍 I'm wondering... (Qiziqyapman...)\n\n📍 I'D LIKE TO KNOW / I WANT TO KNOW:\n  📍 I'd like to know... (Bilmoqchiman...)\n  📍 I want to know... (Bilishni xohlayman...)\n  📍 Please tell me... (Iltimos, ayting...)\n\n📍 ESLATMA: Can you tell me? / Do you know? ? question mark. I wonder ? full stop.",
    "5️⃣ INDIRECT QUESTIONS — SO'Z TARTIBI\n\nIndirect questions da so'z tartibi darak gapdagi kabi (ega + fe'l).\n\n📍 DIRECT: Yordamchi fe'l + ega + asosiy fe'l\n  📍 Where is she? (is + she)\n  📍 What does he want? (does + he + want)\n  📍 When did they arrive? (did + they + arrive)\n\n📍 INDIRECT: So'roq ibora + wh-word + ega + fe'l\n  📍 Can you tell me where she is? (she + is)\n  📍 Do you know what he wants? (he + wants — 'does' yo'q!)\n  📍 I wonder when they arrived. (they + arrived — 'did' yo'q!)\n\n📍 BE FE'LI BILAN:\n  📍 Direct: Is he at home?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know if he is at home? (he is, is he emas)\n\n📍 PRESENT SIMPLE (do/does):\n  📍 Direct: What does he do?\n  📍 Indirect: Can you tell me what he does? (he does, does he emas)\n\n📍 PAST SIMPLE (did):\n  📍 Direct: Where did she go?\n  📍 Indirect: Do you know where she went? (she went, did she go emas)\n\n📍 MUHIM: Indirect qilinganda do/does/did tushib qoladi va fe'l to'g'ri shaklga o'tadi!",
    "6️⃣ INDIRECT QUESTIONS BILAN MULOQOT\n\nIndirect questions kundalik hayotda muloyimlik uchun ishlatiladi.\n\n📍 KO'CHADA YO'L SO'RASH:\n  📍 Excuse me, could you tell me how to get to the station?\n  (Kechirasiz, stansiyaga qanday borishni ayta olasizmi?)\n  📍 Do you know where the nearest bank is?\n  (Eng yaqin bank qayerda ekanligini bilasizmi?)\n\n📍 DO'KON / RESTORANDA:\n  📍 Can you tell me how much this costs?\n  (Bu qancha turishini ayta olasizmi?)\n  📍 I wonder if you have this in a smaller size.\n  (Bu kichikroq o'lchamda bormi, deb o'ylayman)\n  📍 Could you tell me what time you close?\n  (Soat nechada yopishingizni ayta olasizmi?)\n\n📍 ISH / INTERVIEWDA:\n  📍 I'd like to know what the salary is.\n  (Maosh qancha ekanligini bilmoqchiman)\n  📍 Could you tell me what the working hours are?\n  (Ish vaqti qanday ekanligini ayta olasizmi?)\n\n📍 TELEFONDA:\n  📍 Do you know when he will be back?\n  (U qachon qaytishini bilasizmi?)\n  📍 Can you tell me who I should speak to?\n  (Kim bilan gaplashishim kerakligini ayta olasizmi?)",
    "7️⃣ INDIRECT QUESTIONS — UMUMIY XATOLAR VA QOIDALAR\n\nEng keng tarqalgan xatolar va ularning to'g'rilanishi.\n\n📍 DO/DOES/DID ni tushirib qoldirmaslik:\n  ? ? Do you know where does she live? (does xato — indirect da yo'q)\n  ? ? Do you know where she lives?\n\n📍 SO'Z TARTIBINI O'ZGARTIRMASLIK:\n  ? ? Can you tell me where is the station? (savol tartibi)\n  ? ? Can you tell me where the station is? (darak tartibi)\n\n📍 QUESTION MARK:\n  ? 'Can you tell me...' bilan: Can you tell me what time it is? ? (question mark)\n  ? 'I wonder' bilan: I wonder what time it is. ? (full stop)\n\n📍 IF BILAN TO'G'RI ISHLATISH:\n  ? ? Do you know does she like it? (savol shakli)\n  ? ? Do you know if she likes it? (if + subject + verb)\n\n📍 WHETHER BILAN OR NOT:\n  📍 I wonder whether he is coming or not. (or not bilan)\n  📍 I wonder whether he is coming. (or not siz)",
    "8️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR\n\nO'zbek tilida egri so'roqlar va to'g'ri so'roqlar bir xil tuzilishga ega.\n\n📍 O'ZBEK TILIDA:\n  📍 To'g'ri: U qayerda?\n  📍 Egri: Ayta olasizmi, u qayerda?\n  Ikkalasi ham bir xil so'z tartibi (u + qayerda).\n\n📍 INGLIZ TILIDA:\n  📍 Direct: Where is he? (verb + subject)\n  📍 Indirect: Can you tell me where he is? (subject + verb)\n  So'z tartibi o'zgaradi!\n\n📍 ENG KENG TARQALGAN XATOLAR:\n  — Indirect question da savol tartibini saqlash:\n    ? 'Can you tell me where is the station?' ?\n    ? 'Can you tell me where the station is?' ?\n  — Do/does/did ni saqlash:\n    ? 'Do you know where does he work?' ?\n    ? 'Do you know where he works?' ?\n  — If ni tushirish:\n    ? 'Do you know she is coming?' ? (not to'g'ri)\n    ? 'Do you know if she is coming?' ?\n\n📍 AMALIY QOIDA:\n  Direct question ? yordamchi fe'l + ega\n  Indirect question ? ega + fe'l (yordamchi fe'l tushadi)",
  ],
